iio: accel: bmc150: don't touch interrupt info when no IRQ is wired

Without an IRQ the interrupt info is never set up (NULL); enabling the
buffer (iio-sensor-proxy) dereferenced it and oopsed. Newer kernels return
early in this case.

--- a/drivers/iio/accel/bmc150-accel-core.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/accel/bmc150-accel-core.c
@@ -529,6 +529,10 @@
 	const struct bmc150_accel_interrupt_info *info = intr->info;
 	int ret;
 
+	/* No IRQ wired: interrupts were never set up, so there is no info. */
+	if (!info)
+		return 0;
+
 	if (state) {
 		if (atomic_inc_return(&intr->users) > 1)
 			return 0;
